{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-103785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find a vector-valued function $r(u,v)$ that parametrizes the surface defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z={x}^{3}-xy.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ae024b942d2c178c9e2ab625062840cabb3638d8f2be0567152387019ee9a35"} {"question" "q-103785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=x\\,i+y\\,j+z\\,k=x\\,i+y\\,j+({x}^{3}-xy)\\,k.\n$$\n\nNow, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain the vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=u\\,i+v\\,j+({u}^{3}-uv)\\,k\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ae024b942d2c178c9e2ab625062840cabb3638d8f2be0567152387019ee9a35"} {"question" "q-103785" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cffe361c135459c261777ef317ddae9665bbbd907f8873539f00567489831ce6"} {"question" "q-103785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ae024b942d2c178c9e2ab625062840cabb3638d8f2be0567152387019ee9a35"} {"question" "q-103785" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r(u,v)=u\\,i+({u}^{3}-uv)\\,j+v\\,k"] ["math" "r(u,v)=u\\,i+v\\,j+({u}^{3}-uv)\\,k"] ["math" "r(u,v)=uv\\,i+u\\,j+v\\,k"] ["math" "r(u,v)=uv\\,i+v\\,j+u\\,k"] ["math