,v)$ that parametrizes the surface defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z=\\sqrt[3]{x-y}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ae024b942d2c178c9e2ab625062840cabb3638d8f2be0567152387019ee9a35"} {"question" "q-104147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A point $(x,y,z)$ on our surface has the corresponding position vector given by\n\n$$\nr=⟨x,\\,y,\\,z⟩=⟨x,\\,y,\\,\\sqrt[3]{x-y}⟩.\n$$\n\nNow, setting $x=u$ and $y=v,$ we obtain a vector function that parametrizes the surface:\n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\sqrt[3]{u-v}⟩\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ae024b942d2c178c9e2ab625062840cabb3638d8f2be0567152387019ee9a35"} {"question" "q-104147" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "cffe361c135459c261777ef317ddae9665bbbd907f8873539f00567489831ce6"} {"question" "q-104147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14042053/state.json" "file_sha256" "0ae024b942d2c178c9e2ab625062840cabb3638d8f2be0567152387019ee9a35"} {"question" "q-104147" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\sqrt[3]{u+v}⟩"] ["math" "r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\sqrt[3]{u-v}⟩"] ["math" "r(u,v)=⟨u,\\,v,\\,\\sqrt[3]{{u}^{2}-{v}^{2}}⟩"] ["math" "r(u,v)=⟨v,\\,u,\\,u-v⟩"] ["math" "r(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\,{v}^{2},\\,\\sqrt[3]{u+v}⟩"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy